hey what is going on YouTube now I know  a lot of you have already heard about  this but I felt that vlogging about this  topic would only be appropriate now  recently as I'm sure a lot of you guys  already know Robin Williams passed away  and to me he was one of the most  influential greatest comedian actors of  all time and when I found out the news  honestly it was a hard pill to swallow  actually when first hearing it I was in  disbelief and it was a really hard thing  to process because I didn't want to  believe what was being told to me but  when I allowed it to sink in I was  speechless now for those of you who  don't know as more and more information  is being brought out it's becoming more  apparent that the cause of death was  actually suicide now I understand that  this is a very large and heavy topic for  a lot of you to digest but it seems that  a lot of people out there don't  understand or can't grasp the concept of  a stand-up comedian or comedian in  general committing suicide now I know a  lot of you out there are thinking how  could a comedian who's light and art is  based on making other people happy take  his own life how could he not have been  happy himself not when you look at the  surface you only see the stuff that's  apparent you see the long successful  career that he's had the impact that  he's made but then you start to wonder  what was going on through his mind now I  know that this may come as a shock to a  lot of you out there but as a former  stand-up comedian and the current  entertainer yeah Robin Williams passing  was very shocking and surprising but at  the same time I'm not surprised that a  stand-up comedian would do something  like this I'm not saying I knew Robin  Williams on a personal level but what I  am saying is that I can tell you my  perception of comedy and comedians alike  I think a lot of people out there either  forget or you guys just are unaware of  the fact that a lot of the humor that  you relate to and listen to the root of  that comedy comes from a lot of pain and  personal experience you know I've said  this before but I think I'll say it  again comedy is real because it's an art  form that expresses laughter through  pain you know the stories that you hear  the [ __ ] up situation that we've been  in and all the humor that comes from  that comes from a very personal space  it's just that comedians had this  ability to take that anguish and turn it  into something parable which for us is  laughter when I was younger at an early  age I found out that a lot of  times when I was going through a lot of  [ __ ] all I could do was laugh at the  situation and when I did that it just it  took away all the pain you know one of  the reasons why I even became a stand-up  comic in the first place was because I  found out about the power that laughter  had and I wanted to share it  how laughter had a healing property and  it could change a situation by a simple  foot in perception you know in my case  when I was a stand-up comedian I used to  go onstage and grab a mic and I used to  just bust people up laughing and they  would be in tears that was the greatest  joy for me and the reason why was  because I was allowed to share my  personal stories in pain take that and  make them laugh do it it was it was  therapeutic it kind of helped me deal  with my problems but at the same time it  brought other people joy it was it was a  win-win situation and doing that gave me  purpose in the Robin Williams case I  can't help but wonder if at the moment  of his death that he realized how much  his work affected everybody else in the  world and if he didn't and that was the  case how lonely must he have been a lot  of you might not understand this but to  be a comedian that could give life and  value to other people through the comedy  that you make but to not be able to do  that for yourself you know that must  have been terrifying to be honest when  the laughter stops and you can't find  joy through that pain that is exactly  what you're left with pain I can't speak  for other comedians but when I can't  find the joy and laughter and what I do  I don't know what my purpose on this  planet would be I would be lost I  wouldn't know what to do and once again  for those of you out there who aren't  comedians or don't really understand the  comic world I want you to really think  about why you were late to a lot of  these comics who talk about their  personal stories why does it hit so hard  for you at home why does it make you  laugh so much the comedy is real because  the emotion and paint behind the  laughter is real and what you can't  understand that you're not going to be  able to fully grasp the gravity of the  situation even for me I I can't grasp  the whole situation but what I can tell  you as an aspiring actor writer comedian  is that we lost someone very special  that day and Robin I genuinely hope  that you understand how important you  were to a lot of people out there rest  in peace
 

